    <item>
      <title>Looking through the windows: A pragmatic approach for dylib hijacking detection</title>
      <link>https://secopssleuth.github.io/notes/posts/dylib_dll_detection/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 20 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://secopssleuth.github.io/notes/posts/dylib_dll_detection/</guid>
      
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Inspired by Patrick Wardle&amp;rsquo;s talk at &lt;a href=&#34;https://objectivebythesea.org/v8/&#34;&gt;OBTSv8&lt;/a&gt; (Dylib Hijacking on macOS: Dead or Alive?) I wanted to ask the question “What can we learn from DLL hijacking on Windows to improve dylib hijacking detection on macOS?”&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
